{"tool_name":"nanoj","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:nanoj"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"nanoj","home":"https://github.com/HenriquesLab/NanoJ-Core","license":"MIT","summary":"A high-performance open-source super-resolution microscopy toolbox.\n\nNanoJ-Core is an open-source ImageJ and Fiji plugin that provide the base high-performance computing engine that other NanoJ plugins need to run: NanoJ-SRRF, NanoJ-SQUIRREL, NanoJ-VirusMapper and NanoJ-Fluidics.\n\nSuper-Resolution Radial Fluctuations (SRRF) - ImageJ Plugin.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T12:03:09Z","last_update_date":"2021-03-08T09:20:44Z","tool_type":["Plug-in"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:nanoj","credit":[{"name":"Pedro M Pereira","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1426-9540","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Ricardo Henriques","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2043-5234","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Romain F Laine","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2151-4487","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Si\u00e2n Culley","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2112-0143","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Kalina L Tosheva","typeEntity":"Person"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/HenriquesLab/NanoJ-Fluidics/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"},{"term":"Single particle analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3457"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"NanoJ","owner":"Niclaskn","publication":[{"doi":"10.1088/1361-6463/AB0261","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019 IOP Publishing Ltd.Super-resolution microscopy (SRM) has become essential for the study of nanoscale biological processes. This type of imaging often requires the use of specialised image analysis tools to process a large volume of recorded data and extract quantitative information. In recent years, our team has built an open-source image analysis framework for SRM designed to combine high performance and ease of use. We named it NanoJ - a reference to the popular ImageJ software it was developed for. In this paper, we highlight the current capabilities of NanoJ for several essential processing steps: spatiooral alignment of raw data (NanoJ-Core), super-resolution image reconstruction (NanoJ-SRRF), image quality assessment (NanoJ-SQUIRREL), structural modelling (NanoJ-VirusMapper) and control of the sample environment (NanoJ-Fluidics). We expect to expand NanoJ in the future through the development of new tools designed to improve quantitative data analysis and measure the reliability of fluorescent microscopy studies.","authors":[{"name":"Albrecht D."},{"name":"Almada P."},{"name":"Baum B."},{"name":"Culley S."},{"name":"Gray R.D.M."},{"name":"Gustafsson N."},{"name":"Henriques R."},{"name":"Hurtig F."},{"name":"Laine R.F."},{"name":"Leterrier C."},{"name":"Lindas A.-C."},{"name":"Mercer J."},{"name":"Pereira P.M."},{"name":"Risa G.T."},{"name":"Tosheva K.L."}],"citationCount":32,"date":"2019-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Journal of Physics D: Applied Physics","title":"NanoJ: A high-performance open-source super-resolution microscopy toolbox"},"pmcid":"PMC7655149","pmid":"33191949"}],"topic":[{"term":"Allergy, clinical immunology and immunotherapeutics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3400"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Immunology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0804"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}]},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:nanoj/plugin/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":false,"license":true